# The build context is the repo root (`docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .`,
# and `context: .` in every compose file), so this is the file Docker reads —
# it looks beside the context, not beside docker/Dockerfile.
#
# Docker ignore patterns are anchored at the build context root and do not
# recurse on their own — `node_modules` would only match /node_modules. Every
# path that can appear once per workspace package is written `**/`.
#
# What gets through is exactly what `turbo prune --docker` needs to cut the
# workspace: the root manifests, the lockfile, turbo.json, and each package's
# files. The prune stage copies the context whole; anything it would not keep
# is excluded here so it does not bust that layer's cache either.

# Installs and build output, in any package — the image makes its own.
**/node_modules
**/.output
**/.nitro
**/.tanstack
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/coverage
out

# Runtime state and operator files: never inside an image.
data
backups
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Developer and repo tooling the image never reads.
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.impeccable
docs
*.md
!README.md

# drizzle-kit's diff snapshots; the migrator reads only the SQL and the journal.
packages/db/drizzle/**/*.snapshot.json
